<title>GREECE: Athens bourse approves 40 bln drachma EBRD FRN.</title>
<headline>Athens bourse approves 40 bln drachma EBRD FRN.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The board of the Athens stock exchange approved a 40 billion drachma, 5-year European Bank for Reconstruction and Development (EBRD) FRN with interest set at one-month Athibor minus 85 basis points, it said.</p>
<p>The issue would pay interest monthly, it added.</p>
<p>It was unclear which commercial bank was the lead manager but the structure of the issue pointed to a bank with a strong retail network, bankers said.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
